    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p><me>f'(x) = 3x^{2}+12x-63 = 3(x-3)(x+7)</me>
The critical numbers are <m>x = 3</m> and <m>x = -7</m>.</p>
<p>(a) Only the critical number <m>x = -7</m> is in the interval <m>[-8, 0]</m>.
The value of the function at this critical number is
<me>f(-7) = 397</me>
The values at the endpoints are 
<me>f(-8) = 381 \quad \text{and} \quad f(0)=5</me>
Comparing these values we see that:</p>
<p><B> 1. </B>   Absolute maximum = <m>397</m></p>
<p><B> 2. </B> Absolute minimum = <m>5</m>.</p>
<p>(b) Only the critical number <m>x = 3</m> is in the interval <m>[-5, 4]</m>.
The value of the function at this critical number is
<me>f(3) = -103</me>
The values at the endpoints are 
<me>f(-5) = 345 \quad \text{and} \quad f(4)=-87</me>
Comparing these values we see that:</p>
<p><B> 1. </B>   Absolute maximum = <m>345</m></p>
<p><B> 2. </B> Absolute minimum = <m>-103</m>.</p>
<p>(c) Both  critical numbers <m>x = -7</m> and <m>x = 3</m> are in the interval <m>[-8, 4]</m>.
The values of the function at these critical numbers are
<me>f(-7) = 397 \quad \text{and} \quad f(3) = -103</me>
The values at the endpoints are 
<me>f(-8) = 381 \quad \text{and} \quad f(4)=-87</me>
Comparing these values we see that:</p>
<p><B> 1. </B>   Absolute maximum = <m>397</m></p>
<p><B> 2. </B> Absolute minimum = <m>-103</m>.</p>
</solution>
